        <div class="cav">Your drive is not broken</div>
        <h1>Why Does a 1 TB Drive Show Up as <em>Only 931 GB?</em></h1>
        <p class="dek">You buy a 1 TB drive, plug it in, and your computer says 931 GB. Nothing is wrong, and nothing is missing. The drive maker counts in decimal and your operating system counts in binary. Here is what GB and GiB really mean, the exact math behind the 931, and the units the Best Answer Hub Data Storage Converter gets right.</p>
